# upstream/79-operation-equivalence-symbol-hook: OperationEquivalence takes
# a hook giving what stands for each symbol reference, and maps through it
# every reference in an operation's attributes and in the types of its
# results, operands and block arguments, so partition refinement finds two
# functions equal when they differ only in naming members of one class,
# the labels a closure family's type names among them. Built against the
# pinned MLIR (equivalence.cpp): two calls naming @a and @b, two results
# whose tensor types name them, and two uses of those results are
# equivalent and hash alike with @b in @a's class; none is without the
# hook, and naming @c, of a class of its own, is not.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "OperationEquivalence: symbols mapped in attributes, result types and operand types" \
  "$here/equivalence.cpp"
